{
  "title": "About Livecode Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "bb6d3678f2754a6c",
      "text": "The Livecode plugin runs a Livecode wasm stack as a lazy wiki widget. A `livecode` item renders a light poster card; clicking it boots the stack's HTML5 standalone in an iframe. The engine is about 6.4 MB of wasm plus real runtime memory, so at most one widget is live at a time, and a watchdog tears the frame down when the item leaves the lineup."
    },
    {
      "type": "livecode",
      "id": "3b8ba788403d6699",
      "text": "STACK https://wasm.livecode.wiki/assets/wasm/shared/stack.html?zip=hexagon.zip\nTITLE Hexagon\nHEIGHT 460"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "4b7e9d2c8f0a3615",
      "text": "# Commands\nUPPERCASE first word, optional colon, one per line:\n\n- STACK — the standalone's shell page: absolute `https://...` or a path relative to the item's origin site\n- TITLE — the poster label; defaults to the shell file name\n- HEIGHT — iframe height in pixels; defaults to 420\n- BOOT — `click` (default) or `auto`; auto boots on render, use sparingly\n- FULLSCREEN — `fixed` (default), `scale`, or `resize`; how the stack behaves when the full control is used — see [[Full Screen Wasm]]\n- NAME — the stack's name, needed only by `resize` mode for the JavaScript bridge call"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "5c8f0a1d9e2b4736",
      "text": "# Design\nDoor two of [[Three Livecode Doors]]: one shared engine pair per Livecode version is cached by the browser, so many widgets cost one engine download plus a small `standalone.zip` each. Messages the stack posts surface as a `livecodeMessage` event on the widget — the grounding for the [[WikiScript]] stage dialect. See [[Livecode Wasm]] for the export anatomy and the trimmed shell."
    }
  ],
